WHAT: Adds #[arithmetic(unchecked)] to SolDecoder's read_word and read_u8
methods, eliminating redundant overflow checks on ABI cursor advancement.

WHY: read_word does pos + 32 and checks if the result overflowed (pos + 32 < pos).
This check can never trigger because pos is bounded by calldatasize (max ~16KB
in practice). The overflow check generates uaddo instructions that expand to
3-4 EVM opcodes each. For a 32-element array decode, that's 32 unnecessary
overflow checks (64+ wasted opcodes).

GAS IMPACT: -2386 gas total across ALL 16 benchmarked functions. Every single
contract improved.
  governance: -68 to -339 per function (6 functions)
  verifier/plonkVerify: -444
  erc20: -90 to -180
  math: -66 per function (3 functions)
  amm/addLiquidity: -121
  merkle: unchanged (uses calldata directly, not SolDecoder)

CODEGEN IMPACT: Eliminates uaddo instructions from decoder hot paths.
Each uaddo becomes a simple ADD, removing the branch and error handling.

TEAM NOTES: This is the breakthrough that validated the Fe std library
optimization strategy. Changing 2 lines in sol.fe improved ALL contracts
because every contract decodes calldata through SolDecoder. This single
commit produced more gas savings than all 11 sonatina optimizer commits
combined. Key lesson: optimize the hot paths in the std library first.

CROSS-CUTTING: Universal improvement because SolDecoder is used by every
contract's ABI dispatch path.
